`spidergram.sty' provides the features of the spidergram in a convenient style file and as tikzlibrary. 

For details and implementation of the method [Methorst et al, 2026]:
https://en.boerenboom.nl/


For questions regarding the style file or tikzlibrary email me, Carsten Schulz: koryphaeen@posteo.net


How to use

Preamble

\usepackage{tikz}
\usepackage[english]{spidergram}
%included languages options: romanian, dutch, croatian, german, english, latin, finnish, svedish
\usetikzlibrary{spidergram}

%included predefined colors 
\sgcolor{tealblue} %(standard and original color)
%for generation flexibility redefine via one of these
%\sgcolor{bole}
%\sgcolor{byzantinum}
%\sgcolor{sapgreen}
%\sgcolor{vividburgundy}
%\sgcolor{yaleblue}

%the color of the lines in the diagram is defined as:
%\dgcolor{darkgray}


Examples[Baumann et al, n.d.]

Example, Boerenboom (Farming Tree)

\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.6, every node/.style={scale=0.4}]
\boeren{4,4,8,7.5,7,6,5,5,4,9,7,7,6,9,7,8,5,8}
\end{tikzpicture}


Example, Paardenboom (Equine Tree)

\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.6, every node/.style={scale=0.4}]
\paarden{8,9,10,3.5,10,7,6,7,5,7,9,8,9,4,7,9.5,5,8}
\end{tikzpicture}


